# Who Khadi says it is.
#
# os-release(5) format, and in the long run this is what /etc/os-release should
# hold. It cannot be that yet. On Arch /etc/os-release is a symlink owned by the
# `filesystem` package, so putting a real file there picks a fight with pacman on
# every upgrade of it, over a name. Khadi installs this where nothing else claims
# it, and the shell reads it in preference to the base system's.
#
# When Khadi has its own package and its own ISO it will ship this as
# /usr/lib/os-release and the question goes away.
#
# ID_LIKE is the useful half: it tells anything that cares that this is Arch
# underneath, which is true and which scripts rely on.

NAME="Khadi Linux"
PRETTY_NAME="Khadi Linux"
ID=khadi
ID_LIKE=arch
HOME_URL="https://github.com/jhayonline/khadi-linux"
